r loaded | Import it from `catalog.text` instead |\n| `catalog/books.py` | `parse_book` stored the year as a string, which also made `age()` crash | Convert it with `int(year)` |\n| `catalog/factory.py` | Sample data had only Dune and 1984; the docstring and tests expect three books | Added `Book(\"Emma\", \"Austen\", 1815, 1)` |\n| `catalog/fees.py` | The fee was days *plus* the daily rate (`days_late + DAILY_FEE`) | Changed to days *times* the rate (`days_late * DAILY_FEE`) |\n| `catalog/inventory.py` | `recent(n)` returned one event too many (`[-n - 1:]`) | Return `[-n:]`, and an empty list when `n` is 0 or less |\n| `catalog/members.py` | `MAX_BORROWED = 3`, but the comment and tests say five books | Set it to 5 |\n\nThe author and year for Emma aren't checked by the tests (only the title is), so \"Austen, 1815\" is my choice. The guard for `n <= 0` in `recent()` is also an addition of mine: without it, `[-0:]` would return the whole history instead of nothing.", "paced_wait_s": null, "replies_ok": null, "replies_throttled": null, "run_id": "opencode:make-ci-green:claude-opus-5-5:trial1", "sampling_observed": null, "score": 1.0, "success": true, "t_agent_s": 18.834, "t_checker_s": 0.178, "t_env_setup_s": 0.025, "task": "make-ci-green", "timeout_s": 2400, "token_basis": "vendor_split", "token_basis_proxy": null, "tokens": 600, "tokens_cache_read": 17121, "tokens_cache_write": 36446, "tokens_fresh": 600, "tokens_input_uncached": 8, "tokens_output": 592, "tokens_proxy_cache_read": null, "tokens_proxy_cache_write": null, "tokens_proxy_calls": null, "tokens_proxy_input_uncached": null, "tokens_proxy_output": null, "tokens_proxy_reasoning": null, "tokens_reasoning": 0, "trial": 1, "ts_iso": "2026-10-05T01:14:10", "turns": 3, "usage_raw": [{"cache": {"read": 0, "write": 15074}, "input": 4, "output": 101, "reasoning": 0, "total": 15179}, {"cache": {"read": 0, "write": 17121}, "input": 2, "output": 124, "reasoning": 0, "total": 17247}, {"cache": {"read": 17121, "write": 